The AC-2 FastMCP SSE gap is already closed in this tree, so no files were changed. Story 01’s FastAPI app, health probe, and query path are in place, and tool calls go through the official SSE client instead of a mocked `httpx.post`.

`agent/mcp_client.py` calls tools with `mcp.client.sse.sse_client`: GET the SSE URL with `Accept: text/event-stream`, read the session endpoint, then POST JSON-RPC to that session URL. `tests/fastmcp_fake.py` is an in-process peer that rejects a JSON-RPC POST to the SSE URL. `tests/test_tool_call.py` drives that peer and checks the handshake (`initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, `tools/call`) for all four tools.

`/tmp/per20-venv` was used so the `mcp` package was available. The full suite passed: **36 passed**.The background search for an installed `mcp` package was stopped because it was scanning the whole home directory. Dependencies were installed with `uv` instead, and the test suite still passed: 36 tests.
Tool and MCP failures now come back as a clear error. When a tool result contains an `error` field, the agent returns that message directly and stays up. A successful tool result is still synthesized into an answer.

`process_question` checks `tool_result.get("error")` before the second LLM call. A failure such as `{"error": "Employee not found"}` or `{"error": "MCP server unreachable"}` is returned as `{"error": "..."}`. The LLM is not asked to turn that into prose.

