The original stdio agent uppercased every string `id`, so unhyphenated forms like `emp001` were already supported. `_normalize_id()` now does the same thing, and the setup docs show those examples.

The PER-7 stdio orchestrator (`app/agent/orchestrator.py` at `2b12859`) normalized ids with `value.upper()` whenever the argument key was `id`. It did not use a hyphen-only regex. These inputs all went through:

| Input | Sent to the tool |
|---|---|
| `emp-001`, `Emp-001`, `EMP-001` | `EMP-001` |
| `emp001`, `Emp001` | `EMP001` |
| `so-123`, `SO-123` | `SO-123` |
| `so123` | `SO123` |
| `ord-001` | `ORD-001` |

Other argument keys were left unchanged. Hub `requirements.md` was left as-is because the original format was broader than hyphenated `prefix-digits`.

