The AC-2 tool-call test now talks to a real FastMCP SSE server instead of a mocked `httpx.post`.

`tests/test_tool_call.py` starts the `mcp` library's FastMCP SSE app and leaves `sse_client` and `httpx` unpatched. A passing call has to open `GET /sse` with `Accept: text/event-stream`, then post the session to `/messages/`. A JSON-RPC POST straight to the SSE URL never reaches a tool on that server. The same test covers all four tools and checks that `emp-001` and `so-123` arrive as `EMP-001` and `SO-123`.

The FastAPI app, health probe, and Story 01 tests were already in place. The full suite passed: 68 tests.
