The original stdio orchestrator uppercased every string `id` with `value.upper()` when the argument key was `id`. There was no format regex, so `emp001` became `EMP001` the same way `emp-001` became `EMP-001`. `agent/mcp_client.py` still does that, and the README and `tests/test_id_normalization.py` record hyphenated and unhyphenated forms (`emp001`, `so123`, `foo-bar-123`, `emp_001`).

Story 01’s FastAPI app, `GET /health`, and `POST /query` are unchanged. Health still reports the process as up and probes `MCP_URL` with `GET` and `Accept: text/event-stream`, without calling a tool.

